node_modules/
# ⚠️ ANCHORED. A bare `dist/` matches a directory of that name at ANY depth, which once silently
# swallowed a nested build output and shipped it empty, with nothing saying so.
/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Editors
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Build / test output
*.tgz
coverage/
*.log

# Local environment
.env
.env.*

# ⚠️ `CLAUDE.md` and `AGENTS.md` are COMMITTED. They are rendered from `.ds/` by
# `dspec sync --write` and verified against the model — so a clone without them reports a missing
# artifact, and a teammate gets no pointer at the index. Never edit them by hand; regenerate.
#
# ⚠️ So are `.claude/` and `.agents/`, which `dspec init` writes. That is how a teammate gets the
# slash commands on clone. Codex is the exception and cannot be committed: its prompts load only
# from the user's own home directory.
.ds/config.json
CLAUDE.local.md
